---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Dates from "../components/Dates.astro";
import Glance from "@dst/ui/Glance.astro";
import { ICONS } from "@dst/ui/icons";
import { home, origin } from "../content";
import { band, checkedOn } from "../data/band";
import { tourBySlug } from "../data/tours";
import "../data/cities";
import { albumBySlug } from "../data/albums";
import { musicGroup, musicEvent } from "../schema";

const arena = tourBySlug("arena-tour-2026")!;
const summer = tourBySlug("summer-encore-2027")!;
const shows = arena.shows!;
const summerShows = summer.shows!;
const encore = albumBySlug("encore")!;
const canonical = `${origin}/`;

const all = [...shows, ...summerShows];
const countries = [...new Set(all.map((s) => s.country))].length;
const cityCount = [...new Set(shows.map((s) => s.city))].length;

const facts = [
  { label: "Opening night", value: "28 October 2026, London", icon: ICONS.events, href: "/cities/london/" },
  { label: "Last night", value: "23 November 2026, Madrid", icon: ICONS.pin, href: "/cities/madrid/" },
  { label: "Shows", value: `${shows.length} across ${cityCount} cities`, icon: ICONS.stage, href: "/tours/arena-tour-2026/" },
  { label: "Then", value: `${summerShows.length} more, summer 2027`, icon: ICONS.stage, href: "/tours/summer-encore-2027/" },
  { label: "Countries", value: `${countries} across both runs`, icon: ICONS.map, href: "/cities/" },
  { label: "New album", value: "Encore, 16 October 2026", icon: ICONS.play, href: "/albums/encore/" },
  { label: "Last checked", value: checkedOn, icon: ICONS.clock },
];

const jsonLd = [
  musicGroup,
  ...shows.map((show) => musicEvent(show, arena.name, canonical)),
  ...summerShows.map((show) => musicEvent(show, summer.name, canonical)),
];
---
<Layout prose title={home.title} description={home.description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="container hero">
    <h1>{home.h1}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{home.lede}</p>
    <Glance facts={facts} />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Arena Tour 2026</h2>
    <p>
      Seventeen shows in twenty-seven days. Ten countries, eight of the nights in Germany, and one
      city — Paris — that gets the band twice. There is no Americas leg and no second British date.
    </p>
    <p>
      What makes the run worth the notice is the timing. <a href="/albums/encore/">Encore</a>, the
      eighth studio album, is out on 16 October 2026: twelve days before opening night, which makes
      Wembley one of the first rooms anywhere to hear most of it played live.
    </p>
    <Dates shows={shows} />
    <p class="source-line">
      Routing from {arena.source.name}. Last checked {checkedOn}.
      <a href={`/tours/${arena.slug}/`}>More on this tour</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Summer Encore 2027</h2>
    <p>
      There is a second run, and it is the one most listings miss. Fourteen open-air dates from Rome
      on 14 July to Hanover on 27 August 2027 &mdash; four countries, eleven of the fourteen nights
      in Germany, and one of them, on 15 August, in
      {" "}<a href="/cities/magdeburg/">Magdeburg</a>, the city the four of them formed the band in
      twenty-six years earlier.
    </p>
    <p>
      Twelve of the fourteen are on sale with a city and a date and no room yet, which is normal for
      an open-air this far out and is printed here exactly that way rather than filled in.
    </p>
    <Dates shows={summerShows} />
    <p class="source-line">
      Routing from {summer.source.name}. Last checked {checkedOn}.
      <a href={`/tours/${summer.slug}/`}>More on this tour</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The band</h2>
    <p>
      {band.name} formed in {band.origin} in {band.formed}, as {band.formerName}:
      {band.members.map((m, i) => (
        <>{i > 0 && (i === band.members.length - 1 ? " and " : ", ")}{m.name} ({m.role})</>
      ))}. Two of them are twins who had been playing the city since they were ten; the other two
      were in the audience.
    </p>
    <p>
      Twenty-five years later it is still those four people, with nobody replaced &mdash; which is
      the part of the story most bands of that vintage cannot tell.
      <a href="/history/">The whole run of it is here</a>, in dated order.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Where to go next</h2>
    <ul class="next">
      <li><a href="/tours/">Eleven tours since 2005</a> &mdash; including one leg we can document night by night because we published it ourselves in 2015.</li>
      <li><a href="/albums/">Eight studio albums</a> &mdash; dates, labels, and the singles that announced each one.</li>
      <li><a href="/cities/">City by city</a> &mdash; every stop on both runs, and the two cities that are on neither.</li>
      <li><a href="/history/">Twenty-five years in order</a> &mdash; Magdeburg 2001 to Wembley 2026.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .source-line { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .next { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
</style>
